{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega/v5.json",
  "description": "Stacked histogram of Olympic athletes by weight (kg), stacked by sex, in 2kg-wide bins. Fork of the Observable notebook 'Details on demand, stacked histogram/bar chart' (https://observablehq.com/d/9c8c8fc749c73226#cell-1591), originally built with Observable Plot's Plot.rectY(olympians, Plot.binX({y:'count'}, {x:'weight', fill:'sex'})). Data: Observable Plot's own documentation dataset, athletes.csv (Rio 2016 Olympics), pre-aggregated into 2kg weight bins by sex. Written directly in Vega (not Vega-Lite) so the tracked signal (highlight) is backed by a real signal value rather than Vega-Lite's internal `_store` dataset, which reVISit's replay mechanism cannot repopulate. revisitAnswer rides on the existing legend-click interaction (responseId \"stackedbar-value-hover\", with no matching \"response\" entry in config.json).",
